@startuml
title High-Level Design (HLD) - College Record Processing Pipeline

actor User
participant "FastAPI (Backend Service)" as API
participant "Celery Task Queue" as Celery
participant "MongoDB (StageRecords)" as MongoDB
participant "AWS S3" as S3
participant "AWS Textract" as Textract
participant "Processing Pipeline" as Pipeline

User -> API: Submit Job (Single College / Folder)
API -> S3: Fetch Input Files (PDF, unsan.txt, config.json)
API -> Celery: Dispatch Job to Process College
Celery -> Pipeline: Start Processing Pipeline
Pipeline -> Textract: Extract Tables from PDF Images
Pipeline -> S3: Store Extracted Data (Tables, Images)
Pipeline -> MongoDB: Match Extracted Data with StageRecords
Pipeline -> S3: Store Merged JSON Results (Master + MongoDB)
Pipeline -> API: Update Progress Status
API -> MongoDB: Query Processing Status
API -> User: Return Job Status

note right of API
FastAPI Routes:
1. /submit-job (Process Single College)
2. /process-folder (Process All Colleges)
3. /progress (Monitor Progress)
4. /job-status (Check Task Status)
end note

note right of Pipeline
Processing Stages:
1. PDF to Images (Textract)
2. Table Extraction (Textract)
3. BLEU Score Matching (Unsan vs Extracted)
4. Merge with MongoDB (Master JSON)
5. Upload Final Output to S3
end note

@enduml
